iza.7", "J.M.Raimond.1", "K.M.FonsecaRomero.1", "C.E.Clayton.1", "M.Brune.1", "J.Dreyer.1", "J.G.Peixoto.de.Faria.2"], "figures": [{"filename": "eta0.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Correlation signal $\\eta(t)$ for $k/\\gamma=0$ (full line) and $k/\\gamma=0.01$ (dashed line) for ${|\\alpha(0)|}^{2}=3.3$ and $\\phi=0.98rad$.", "label": "fig1", "source": "arxiv", "key": "ac90525b411f66dba71de48eb1229dd4", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/ac90525b411f66dba71de48eb1229dd4"}, {"filename": "deco098.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Same as Figure 1 for the linear entropy $\\delta(t)$.", "label": "fig2", "source": "arxiv", "key": "1974b0b19805c9459b0fdeb458e284c6", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/1974b0b19805c9459b0fdeb458e284c6"}, {"filename": "eta04.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Correlation signal $\\eta(t)$ for $k/\\gamma=0$ (full line) and $k/\\gamma=0.01$ (dashed line) for ${|\\alpha(0)|}^{2}=3.3$ and $\\phi=0.4rad$.", "label": "fig4", "source": "arxiv", "key": "642250285a0bb482dab72a4cb526f5ea", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/642250285a0bb482dab72a4cb526f5ea"}, {"filename": "deco04.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Same as Figure 3 for the linear entropy $\\delta(t)$.", "label": "fig5", "source": "arxiv", "key": "dc44099c472c3680f65af1b8b3cb6c6e", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/dc44099c472c3680f65af1b8b3cb6c6e"}, {"filename": "eta0405.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Correlation signal for the case in figure 3, but $k/\\gamma-0.05$.", "label": "fig6", "source": "arxiv", "key": "055c95ebf7d22105faf8f0cc23d226f2", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/055c95ebf7d22105faf8f0cc23d226f2"}, {"filename": "deco0405.png", "material": "preprint", "caption": "Linear entropy for the case in figure 3, but $k/\\gamma-0.05$.", "label": "fig7", "source": "arxiv", "key": "891dd9c35a3b284b5c6d169dd90f8b01", "url": "https://inspirehep.net/files/891dd9c35a3b284b5c6d169dd90f8b01"}], "inspire_categories": [{"term": "Quantum Physics", "source": "arxiv"}], "preprint_date": "2001-06-08", "author_count": 3, "first_author": {"full_name": "Mokarzel, S.G.", "last_name": "Mokarzel", "first_name": "S.G.", "recid": 2976615}, "public_notes": [{"source": "arXiv", "value": "13 pages, 6 figures"}], "control_number": 3031534, "dois": [{"material": "publication", "source": "arXiv", "value": "10.1103/PhysRevA.65.044101"}], "earliest_date": "2001-06-08", "document_type": ["article"], "texkeys": ["Mokarzel:2001yse"], "abstracts": [{"source": "arXiv", "value": "A model is presented to describe the recently proposed experiment (J. Raimond, M. Brune and S. Haroche Phys. Rev. Lett {\\bf 79}, 1964 (1997)) where a mesoscopic superposition of radiation states is prepared in a high-Q cavity which is coupled to a similar resonator. The dynamical coherence loss of such state in the absence of dissipation is reversible and can in principle be observed. We show how this picture is modified due to the presence of the environmental couplings. Analytical expressions for the experimental conditional probabilities and the linear entropy are given. We conclude that the phenomenon can still be observed provided the ratio between the damping constant and the inter-cavities coupling does not exceed about a few percent. This observation is favored for superpositions of states with large overlap.", "abstract_source_suggest": {"input": "arXiv"}}], "primary_arxiv_category": ["quant-ph"], "titles": [{"source": "arXiv", "title": "Modelling the Recoherence of Mesoscopic Superpositions in Dissipative Environments"}], "facet_author_name": ["2290004_A.N. Salgueiro", "995880_Maria Carolina Nemes", "2976615_S.G. Mokarzel"], "_oai": {"sets": ["Literature"], "id": "oai:inspirehep.net:3031534", "updated": "2025-10-02T16:30:05.432826"}, "curated": false, "arxiv_eprints": [{"categories": ["quant-ph"], "value": "quant-ph/0106044"}]}, "created": "2025-10-02T16:30:02.356863+00:00", "updated": "2025-10-02T16:30:05.432826+00:00", "links": {"bi